course: dictionary
lesson: 10659
title: Unkindness and its shades
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unkindness means being unkind: mean, cruel or hurtful to others. The ending -ness turns the adjective unkind into a noun, a name for the quality. Unkind means not kind, so unkindness is the state of not being kind.
explain: Sometimes unkindness is one act or one word. Then we say an unkindness, with a small a, and the plural is unkindnesses. «Must be nice» said quietly about a friend's holiday is a small unkindness when it is said to hurt, not just a passing feeling.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is used. If a sentence describes how people treat each other, unkindness is the general state. If it names one thing someone did or said, it is a single unkindness.
fact: Unkindness means being unkind, mean or cruel to others.
fact: An unkindness is one unkind act or word.
fact: Unkindness is the opposite of kindness.
fact: Unkindness hurts feelings, even when nobody shouts or hits anyone.
fact: You can say an act of unkindness or unkindness to animals.
exercise: «Paying a frenemy back with the same unkindness usually makes two frenemies and two unhappy people.» What does unkindness mean here? | Giving someone a present | *Being mean or cruel back to someone | Forgetting a birthday | Singing very loudly
exercise: Ella says, «It was an unkindness to leave Sam out of the game.» What is an unkindness? | A type of game | The whole of being unkind | *One unkind act | A kind thing to do
exercise: Which is the correct plural of an unkindness? | unkindness | *unkindnesses | unkinds | unkindnesss
test: «Must be nice» said quietly about a friend's holiday is a small bit of jealousy. Why can it turn into unkindness? | It is always kind, so it never can | *If it is said to make the friend feel bad | If the friend is ill | If it is said about the weather
test: Which sentence uses unkindness to mean the general state of being unkind? | *Unkindness hurts people. | Unkindnesses are a game. | She has three unkindness. | An unkindness hurt her.
exam: «The myth was convenient, and convenient myths can hide unkindness.» What does unkindness suggest in this sentence? | *Mean or cruel behaviour that stays hidden | Kindness to a friend | A loud noise | A holiday in the sun
